# Phantom Fudge TODO Index

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Entire v1 lifecycle
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Create a complete, evidence-backed Windows 11 speaker-notes application, starting with a
capture proof rather than assuming a window can be universally undetectable.

## Current state

- Implementation authorized October 8. Local experimental implementation is now in progress.
- User approved Windows 11 first with Teams, Zoom, Google Meet, and OBS qualified separately.
- Start the proposed opaque WPF/C#/.NET 10 design; four-product qualification still blocks release.
- Live meeting-output transcription and its local Docker service are REQUIRED workstreams 19 and 20.
- Local synthetic GDI/UI/speech evidence and approved hardware-loopback recognition exist.
- No four-product qualification, actual Docker execution, owner UX acceptance, commit, push or public release.
- WORKFLOWS statuses describe authored procedures, not app execution.

## Next action

Use docs\PREVIEW-GUIDE.md for the native development candidate. Owner installs/starts Docker Desktop,
then task20 can run its actual container checks. Complete required product/hardware/UX qualification
before promoting this preview. Tasks19/20 remain mandatory, not future work.

## Status values

- NOT_STARTED - Planned, not implemented/executed.
- IN_PROGRESS - Active work or partly resolved decisions, with current evidence.
- BLOCKED - Named missing decision, dependency, access, device, or approval.
- DONE - Every scoped task and acceptance criterion met with evidence.

Dependencies are completion prerequisites. Unstarted dependent work is NOT_STARTED; a
concrete attempted-work blocker is BLOCKED and must name the owner/action. See
..\docs\TODO-CONVENTIONS.md for the full update and completion contract.

